From 690e4d31ae8ee7b00a85f9f0b9e67dbcada37b56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:42:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] portal: add a safe custom CSS editor (Hotspot > Portal)

Operators can restyle the captive portal from the Portal admin page without
being able to break it.

Portal (hotspot/):
- index.html loads the operator CSS as its OWN stylesheet after the built-in
  styles (cgi-bin/portal_css.sh), so a mistake can only affect the custom
  rules, never the stock stylesheet.
- On-device safety check: if the CSS hides, shrinks, covers, pushes off-screen
  or blanks the voucher box + Submit, Insert Coin, Resume Time, the main
  panel, or the buttons of an open coin/rates window, on two checks in a row,
  the stylesheet is dropped for that visit (sessionStorage) and the stock look
  is used. Nothing is written server-side; www2 never loads the CSS, so the
  admin can always get back in.  ?nocss=1 forces safe mode.
- ?cssprev=1 (only inside an iframe) enables the admin preview hooks and
  blocks login/logout/coin start/cancel so the preview can't change state.

Admin (www2/):
- hotspot-portal.html: Custom CSS card with editor, live validation, the real
  portal in an iframe (Login / Connected / Rates / Coin, Dark / Light), a
  "check all screens" audit, starter snippets, Undo, Reset, on/off switch.
- hotspot.cgi: portal_css_{info,get,draft,save,enable,revert,reset}.
  Validation rejects unclosed braces/comments, @import, image-set(), script-
  capable CSS, control chars, >24 KB, and url() to anything but /img/,
  /graphics/ or data:image (external files would stall a walled-garden portal).
  Saves are atomic (write+verify then mv), keep the previous version for
  Undo, honour the existing 3 MB free-space floor, and cross-check a client
  byte count so a truncated body can never be saved.

Storage: hotspot_data/portal_custom.css (+ .prev, .off). It lives beside the
other operator data, not in hotspot/, so OTA and module reinstalls leave it
alone with no changes to ota.sh / module_ctl.sh.
