From f44b7642af8894aa09e4588b8ac1779ce43bef08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:09:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] site survey: keep the JSON valid for SSIDs with control
 characters

The survey awk programs build JSON from the scan of OTHER people's access
points. escape_json() handled \ and " but not control characters, and an SSID
may contain any byte, so a nearby device broadcasting a tab or a 0x01-0x1f /
DEL byte made the response invalid JSON: JSON.parse failed and the survey page
went blank for the admin. Replace those bytes with a space first, in both the
sitesurvey_load and sitesurvey_scan programs.

Not an XSS: sitesurvey.html and index.html already escape every ssid they
insert (text context only; the Connect button carries an index, not the SSID).
This only fixes the denial of the survey page by a nearby broadcaster.

Verified by extracting both awk programs verbatim from the original and the
patched CGI and running them under BusyBox 1.36.1 awk on a scan result with a
tab, \001, a quote, a backslash and HTML in an SSID: original output fails
json.loads, patched output parses, markup preserved as data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 www2/cgi-bin/lme.cgi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/www2/cgi-bin/lme.cgi b/www2/cgi-bin/lme.cgi
index 5bacc79..7396378 100755
--- a/www2/cgi-bin/lme.cgi
+++ b/www2/cgi-bin/lme.cgi
@@ -812,6 +812,11 @@ function clean(s) {
     return s
 }
 function escape_json(s) {
+    # SSID text comes from OTHER access routers (not ours): any byte is
+    # possible. Raw control characters (tab, 0x01..0x1f, DEL) are illegal inside
+    # a JSON string and made JSON.parse fail, blanking the survey for the admin
+    # -- turn them into spaces first.
+    gsub(/[\001-\037\177]/, " ", s)
     gsub(/\\/, "\\\\", s); gsub(/"/, "\\\"", s)
     return s
 }
@@ -896,6 +901,11 @@ function clean(s) {
     return s
 }
 function escape_json(s) {
+    # SSID text comes from OTHER access routers (not ours): any byte is
+    # possible. Raw control characters (tab, 0x01..0x1f, DEL) are illegal inside
+    # a JSON string and made JSON.parse fail, blanking the survey for the admin
+    # -- turn them into spaces first.
+    gsub(/[\001-\037\177]/, " ", s)
     gsub(/\\/, "\\\\", s); gsub(/"/, "\\\"", s)
     return s
 }
-- 
