From 24cddd57b208467f0ebe5d0cad18eab2717cba7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:47:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] hotspot QoS: queue discipline dropdown (auto / fq_codel
 / sfq), fq_codel via sch_fq_codel.ko

Adds Hotspot > Bandwidth & QoS > Queue Discipline, which selects the qdisc
under each client's Band 1 / Band 2 HTB leaves:

- auto (default): fq_codel when usable, otherwise sfq
- fq_codel: forced; no sfq substitution - if it cannot be used the leaves
  stay on plain FIFO and the admin page says so
- sfq: forced (the previous behaviour)

lmehspt.sh:
- qos_qdisc_resolve() runs at the top of setup_qos(). It probes fq_codel on
  lo with the same option shape the leaves use, insmods
  /lmepisowifi/sch/sch_fq_codel.ko only if the probe fails, and probes
  again. Failure reasons separate "kernel has no fq_codel" from "tc too old
  for fq_codel options". Result is published to /tmp/hotspot_qdisc_status.
- _qos_add_leaf() attaches the leaf; in auto a failing fq_codel add falls
  back to sfq for that queue, in forced fq_codel it does not.
- fq_codel options scale with the client's guaranteed rate: limit as a
  ~200 ms memory backstop, target >= 1.5 MTU of serialisation time (min
  5 ms), interval = 100 ms + 2 x target, 32 / 128 flows for VIP / bulk.
- The unauthenticated buckets (990:, 299:) stay on sfq: they rely on its
  limit 12 and the per-IP flow-hash emulation.
- QOS_QDISC is dumped into coin_config.env so write_coin_config() does
  not reset it.

hotspot.cgi: QOS_QDISC strict-enum validation in cfg_val_ok (it lands in
root-sourced files); config_get returns qos_qdisc, qos_qdisc_active and
qos_qdisc_note; config_set accepts qos_qdisc.

hotspot.html: Queue Discipline select + a status line showing the active
qdisc and any fallback reason (textContent only; the note can carry
insmod output).

Packaging: sch/ was never shipped. Added it to the base and hotspot-module
tarballs (release.yml), to ota.sh COMPONENTS, and to module_ctl.sh
hotspot_files().

defaults.env: QOS_QDISC="auto".

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
